flowchart TB
    accTitle: Proposed comparison data and trusted policy remain separate
    accDescr: A pull request's proposed head supplies comparison data. The privileged applying route takes instructions and referenced templates only from an immutable trusted base, a deliberately pinned revision, or built-in policy. Proposed policy has no route into privileged instruction execution.

    proposed("Proposed pull request head")
    comparison("Comparison data"):::focus
    proposedPolicy("Proposed policy and templates"):::bad

    subgraph writer["Privileged applying route"]
        policyChoice{"Choose trusted instruction source"}
        trusted("Trusted base or pinned revision")
        builtin("Built-in policy")
        analyze("Analyze proposed changes")
        apply("Apply declared effects under host authority"):::ok
    end

    proposed -->|"supplies patch, files, and source identity"| comparison
    proposed -->|"may contain"| proposedPolicy
    proposedPolicy -.->|"not an instruction source"| blocked("No privileged policy route"):::bad
    trusted -->|"trusted policy and referenced templates"| policyChoice
    builtin -->|"trusted no-config instructions"| policyChoice
    policyChoice -->|"selects the question"| analyze
    comparison -->|"read as data"| analyze
    analyze -->|"desired effects plus bound source identity"| apply
